 "text": "Goals don't die at the start, they die in the middle. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 27. A year to speak Spanish, month 1 every new word feels like a win. Month 6 today's 10 words feel like nothing so you skip a week. At the start you measure from zero, near the end the finish pulls you, in the middle you're far from both. So give the year 12 finish lines. Finish line 1 order dinner in Spanish, 4 weeks away so it pulls. Count the smaller number, first half count what's done, second half count what's left. Now month 6 isn't the middle, it's finish line 6. Send this to the friend stuck halfway through something big. That's what demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, next, why a new goal feels better than the old one. Which goal are you halfway through? The links in the bio.",
